# --- compose (the local stack, twelve files) --------------------------------
#
# Measured: 7 partially adopted, 2 absent, 0 current. The packet's "differs by
# ~450 lines" is confirmed and is the smallest of the numbers here — the
# headline is not the size of the diff, it is that NOT ONE service has the
# stack.
#
# The measurement that matters: of the twelve files kit ships, the fleet holds
# `docker-compose.yml` in seven services and `.env.example` in two. The
# collector, the three trace/metric stores and the Grafana provisioning are
# **0 for 12 across all nine services**. The reporter says "partially adopted"
# rather than reporting eleven separate cells and calling the seven successes
# adoption.
#
# WHAT THESE ARE, AND IT IS NOT "A BROKEN STACK". Checked, because the first
# draft of this file said "so it cannot start" and that was a guess dressed as a
# measurement:
#
#   $ grep -cE '\./(otel-collector|tempo|loki|mimir|grafana)' */docker-compose.yml
#   billing 0  courier 0  darkroom 0  guard 0  identity 0  muse 0
#   $ grep -cE '^\s+- \./' templates/compose/docker-compose.yml
#   5
#
# None of the seven mounts a single one of kit's eleven files. They declare ONE
# OR TWO SERVICES (`db`, `app`, `postgres`, `guard`, `identity`) and they are
# not kit's stack with pieces removed — they are REPLACEMENTS that kept a
# filename. `docker compose config` is GREEN on five of the seven, so they are
# valid, runnable stacks. They are simply not this one.
#
# So the honest reason is the boring one: these seven predate kit's
# observability profile, nobody re-copied, and nobody recorded a decision. That
# is a backlog entry, which is what this file is for.
#
# ONE REAL DEFECT THE BYTE-COMPARISON CANNOT SEE, recorded here because the
# ledger is where a service's owner will look: `muse/docker-compose.yml` DOES NOT
# PARSE. `docker compose config` fails with `yaml: line 65, column 67: mapping
# values are not allowed in this context` — an unquoted `${MUSE_VAULT_KEY:?set …,
# or run: …}` whose error message contains a colon. The reporter calls that cell
# `diverged`, which is true and is not the interesting thing about it.

